## 10. Capabilities (enabled for this client)
Optional platform components, toggled at stamp time (`cap_*` in copier). Only the ones you enabled render.
[% if cap_vector_db %]
### pgvector (`cap_vector_db`)
The `vector` extension is created in `appdb` at cluster bootstrap (`spec.bootstrap.initdb.postInitApplicationSQL`
in `clusters/platform-config/database/cluster.yaml`). Use it from the app's normal `DATABASE_URL` —
`CREATE TABLE ... (embedding vector(1536))`, then an `ivfflat`/`hnsw` index. Notes:
- Runs **once, on a fresh cluster.** To add pgvector to an already-bootstrapped DB, run
  `CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector` once as a superuser (pgvector is untrusted; `appuser` can't).
- Needs a pgvector-capable image. CNPG's default (standard-flavor) images bundle it; a `minimal` image does not.
[% endif %]
[% if cap_db_app_role %]
### Two-role DB / RLS runtime role (`cap_db_app_role`)
The app connects at runtime as **`app_rw`** — a least-privilege, non-owner role that can
`SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE` but run no DDL. Schema migrations run out-of-band as the **owner**
(`appuser`) through the backend PreSync migration Job. Because `app_rw` is non-owner + non-superuser
(CNPG creates it `NOBYPASSRLS`), any Postgres **row-level security** the app declares is enforced against it.
- **Files** (`clusters/platform-config/database/`): the `app_rw` managed role in `cluster.yaml`;
  `app-rw-credentials` (basic-auth → CNPG); `[< client_name >]-db-app-rw` (the app's connection Secret —
  `uri` + discrete `host`/`port`/`dbname`/`username`/`password`); `app-rw-grants-job` (PostSync, grants read-write).
- **Contract:** the runtime Deployment reads `[< client_name >]-db-app-rw` (`uri`); the migration Job keeps the
  owner secret `[< client_name >]-db-app`. Apps taking discrete `DB_*` vars map them to the Secret's discrete keys
  and set `DB_MIGRATIONS_RUN=false` (migrations are the Job's job, as the owner).
- **RLS is yours to declare:** this provisions the *enforcing role* + grants, not policies. The app's migrations
  must `ALTER TABLE ... ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` and add policies. Tables are owned by `appuser`; the owner
  bypasses RLS by default (fine — migrations only). Add `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` only if the owner must be subject too.
- **Secret:** `APP_DB_RW_PASSWORD` in Infisical (URL-safe; see §1.2). Missing → the role never reconciles and
  the grants Job backs off.
[% endif %]
[% if cap_single_writer %]
### Single-writer worker (`cap_single_writer`)
In-process schedulers (`@nestjs/schedule` and friends) fire on **every** replica, so a `@Cron` on the
2-replica web Deployment double-fires — double payouts/purges/races for a money app. This runs the
scheduler in exactly one place: `clusters/apps/backend/base/worker-deployment.yaml` (`backend-worker`,
**replicas: 1**, **strategy: Recreate**), same image/tag as the web backend (the overlay's `images:`
transformer bumps both). Web pods get `SCHEDULER_ENABLED=false`; the worker gets `true`.
- **App contract:** gate the scheduler on `SCHEDULER_ENABLED == "true"` (e.g. don't register
  `ScheduleModule`/`@Cron` unless set). Without that gate the web pods still run crons and the split is moot.
- **Why Recreate, not RollingUpdate:** a rolling update briefly runs the new worker pod alongside the old
  → two schedulers for a few seconds → a tick can double-fire. Recreate stops the old pod first (a short
  scheduler gap on each deploy — acceptable for crons; correctness beats uptime here).
- **Never scale it** and never attach an HPA — `replicas: 1` is the invariant. No Service points at it;
  it exists only to run the scheduler (probes still hit the pod's own `:8080`).
- For stronger guarantees (no scheduler gap, or work that must survive a pod restart mid-run), move the
  schedule out of the app into k8s `CronJob`s (`concurrencyPolicy: Forbid`) invoking a command — heavier,
  needs per-task entrypoints; deferred.
[% endif %]
[% if cap_event_bus %]
### NATS event bus (`cap_event_bus`)
NATS + JetStream (3-node HA, persistent streams) in the `messaging` namespace
(`clusters/platform/72-nats.yaml`). Connect in-cluster at `nats://nats.messaging.svc.cluster.local:4222`.
- **Admin-only, no auth** — the cluster/tailnet is the boundary (same posture as Valkey). Add accounts/nkeys
  before exposing it beyond in-cluster clients.
- JetStream PVC defaults to 2Gi/pod — bump `config.jetstream.fileStore.pvc.size` in the Application for real stream volume.
- Inspect: `kubectl -n messaging exec -it deploy/nats-box -- nats stream ls` (the chart ships a `nats-box`).
[% endif %]
[% if cap_preview_envs %]
### Preview environments (`cap_preview_envs`)
An ArgoCD `ApplicationSet` (`clusters/platform/95-preview-envs.yaml`) with a GitHub **pullRequest** generator
stamps one app per OPEN PR against `[< registry_org >]/[< client_name >]-backend`: namespace `preview-pr-<n>`,
image `sha-<head_short_sha>`, URL `https://pr-<n>.[< domain >]`. Closing the PR prunes the Application + namespace.
- **One-time setup:**
  - Infisical (client path): `PREVIEW_GITHUB_TOKEN` (PR read on the app repo), `PREVIEW_DATABASE_URL`
    (a shared preview/staging `postgres://` URI). `GHCR_USERNAME`/`GHCR_PULL_TOKEN` are reused.
  - DNS: add a **wildcard** `*.[< domain >]` (or `*.preview.[< domain >]`) → the ingress LB, and a DNS-01
    **wildcard cert**, so `pr-<n>.[< domain >]` resolves + serves TLS.
  - App-repo CI must push `ghcr.io/[< registry_org >]/[< client_name >]-backend:sha-<short-sha>` on PR commits
    (extend `build-and-bump`, which already tags `sha-<short-sha>` on main).
- **Shared-DB trade-off:** every preview points at `PREVIEW_DATABASE_URL`. Fine for read-mostly PR review;
  a PR that migrates schema affects all previews. For isolation, give each PR its own CNPG `Cluster`
  (add a per-PR `Cluster` + point the preview `[< client_name >]-db-app` ExternalSecret at it) — deferred follow-up.
- **Gate to labelled PRs** (avoid a preview per PR): uncomment `labels: ["preview"]` in the generator.
- To repoint previews at a different app, edit `clusters/apps/preview/base` + the ApplicationSet `repo`.
[% endif %]
[% endif %]
## [% if cap_vector_db or cap_event_bus or cap_preview_envs or cap_db_app_role or cap_single_writer %]11[% else %]10[% endif %]. Gotchas quick-reference
- **Hetzner server types vary by location + stock** (`cpx41` isn't sold in nbg1; run `hetzner-server-types.sh`).
- **`tofu destroy` leaves the CCM ingress LB** (orphan, still billing) — delete via API after.
- **external-dns `txt-owner-id` must be unique per cluster** or two clusters sharing a Cloudflare zone
  delete each other's records.
- **One Slack webhook = all clusters page it** — silence/tear down dev clusters before an e2e elsewhere.
- **oauth2-proxy cookie secret** must be 16/24/32 bytes (`openssl rand -hex 16`).
